@startuml retention-v2-old-reader
' ============================================================================
' Opening a durable catalog after the first V2 publication (task 7923): the
' reader behaviour that formal/tlaplus/stack_safe_pda/RSpaceRetentionV2Upgrade.tla
' checks, with the four negative controls that each break one decision.
'   GREY   #616161  catalog selection, which reads only the unchanged envelope
'   BLUE   #1565C0  reading the appointed retention object
'   AMBER  #EF6C00  V1 content, which every reader adopts
'   GREEN  #2E7D32  V2 content, which only a dual reader adopts
'   RED    #C62828  refusals, all terminal; and the mutants' stale adoptions
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #455A64
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFE0B2
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #EF6C00
skinparam NoteBorderColor #455A64

title <b>Opening a catalog under the shared retention V2 format</b>\nselection reads only the envelope, the appointed object decides, and a refusal never falls back

start
:Parse both catalog slots:
CRC, domain, version, reserved bytes, flags,
commit length and the slot fields; <<#E0E0E0>>
if (Is any slot valid?) then (no)
  :Refuse: NoValidCatalog; <<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:Select the newest valid slot.
V2 changes no envelope byte, so a V1-only
reader and a dual reader select the same slot; <<#E0E0E0>>
note right #FFEBEE
  <b>CatalogEnvelopeMutant</b>: a V2 publication changes the
  envelope; the V1-only reader cannot parse the new slot,
  selects the older one and adopts its stale V1 state.
  <b>SelectionDivergenceMutant</b>: selection consults the
  appointed format, so the two readers select different slots.
end note
:Read the object the retention reference appoints; <<#BBDEFB>>
switch (Domain of the appointed object?)
case (RSpaceDAG.Retn)
  :Parse the V1 manifest and adopt the
  selected state (every reader); <<#FFE0B2>>
case (RSpaceDAG.RetA)
  if (Does the reader support V2?) then (dual reader)
    :Parse the anchor, unfold the radix history,
    check the count and adopt the selected state; <<#C8E6C9>>
  else (V1-only reader)
    :Refuse: UnknownObjectDomain, or
    InvalidDomain(RSpaceDAG.Retn); <<#FFCDD2>>
    note right #FFEBEE
      Terminal: the reader never falls back to the older slot.
      <b>FallbackOnUnsupportedMutant</b>: it adopts the older
      slot's stale state instead.
      <b>AdoptUnsupportedMutant</b>: it adopts the V2 state
      without checking the format.
    end note
  endif
endswitch
stop
@enduml
